course: dictionary
lesson: 12447
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning the author wants by reading the words around it. Those words are the context, and they are the clue. «Dedicated» is a good example because it has several meanings.
explain: «Mia is a dedicated swimmer. She trains every morning before school.» Dedicated means working very hard at something because you care about it a lot. The clues are trains every morning and before school: Mia is not just interested, she is committed.
explain: «This dedicated cycle lane is only for bikes.» Here dedicated means used for one purpose only. The clue is the word only. Ask yourself what the sentence needs, then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Dedicated can also mean given in someone's honour, as in «The book is dedicated to my grandad.» The author is saying the book is for him. Read the whole sentence, and the meaning is usually clear.
fact: Dedicated is an adjective: «a dedicated pupil», «a dedicated fan».
fact: Dedicate is the verb: «I dedicate this song to my sister.»
fact: «Dedicated» means working very hard at something because you care about it a lot.
fact: «Dedicated» can mean used only for one purpose, as in «a dedicated cycle lane».
fact: «Dedicated» can mean given to God or named after a saint, as in «a dedicated church».
exercise: «Ravi is a dedicated coach who never misses a training session.» What does dedicated mean here? | *Working very hard because he cares a lot | Very tired and sleepy | Given to a saint in a ceremony | Used only for one purpose
exercise: «This dedicated cycle lane is only for bikes.» What does dedicated mean here? | Very wet and muddy | Working very hard at something | Named after a saint | *Used only for one purpose
exercise: The book says, «Dedicated to my mother.» What does dedicated mean here? | *Written in honour of someone | Working very hard at writing it | Used only for one purpose | Lost in the post
test: «The little chapel was dedicated to Saint Brigid.» What does dedicated mean here? | *Given to God or named after a saint | Painted bright blue | Working very hard | Used only for prayers at night
test: What part of speech is dedicated in «a dedicated fan»? | *Adjective | Noun | Verb | Adverb
exam: Which sentence uses dedicated to mean given in someone's honour? | *«She dedicated her song to her gran.» | «The dedicated lane is for buses only.» | «He is a dedicated reader who reads every night.» | «The dedicated machine is in the science lab.»
